# Secrets and personal network details never go in git. For every ignored file
# below there is a committed `.example` template showing its structure.

# Real per-machine settings (hostname, username, timezone, ...)
*.env
!*.env.example

# cloud-init files written onto the SD card contain a password hash and an SSH
# public key. The committed template is base/user-data.example.
user-data
meta-data
network-config

# Backups made by the card-patching scripts may contain the real user-data.
backup-*/
pi-card-backup-*/

# Private keys, just in case something is copied into the repo by mistake.
id_*
!id_*.pub.example
*.pem
*.key
